\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Work out the details of showing that this is valid. For example, we need to know that if #{f : A \to B} is a bijection then we can use it to make a bijection between #{A \times C} and #{B \times C}; we also need to know that chaining two bijections together will give another bijection.}
